<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Output src/glueball.rs. std only. Zero-momentum 0++ glueball operators for SU(2) on a torus with one Euclidean time direction time_dir. ape_step(torus, links, time_dir, alpha): spatial links become P[(1-alpha) U + alpha/(2(d-2)) sum of the 2(d-2) spatial staples (paths x -> x+mu through x+nu and x-nu)], P = division by the quaternion norm; time links unchanged. slice_plaquettes: average a0 over spatial plaquettes per time slice. smeared_slice_operators(torus, links, time_dir, alpha, steps): slice operators after each cumulative number of APE steps. correlator(series, mean): connected C(t), t = 0..nt/2, averaged over source slices. Independent tests in tests/glueball.rs: smearing keeps SU(2) and leaves time links unchanged; slice operators gauge invariant to 1e-12 after a random gauge transformation; cold configuration gives 1; C(0) equals the variance. The GPU driver is examples/glueball_gpu.rs (effective masses with jackknife, reference Teper hep-th/9812187 Table 10).
